@page "/"

@*
    The front page. Markup without a ViewModel, because the page fetches no data — it must be able
    to be shown even when the database is down, so the way to /book never closes. The one piece of
    interactivity, the map of the neighbourhood, is its own component with its own render mode, so
    this page still renders as static HTML when the circuit is gone.

    The content follows the mockup NFHotel-Forside-Mockup.html (2026-11-03). The facts of the
    hotel's own page (24-hour bar, kitchen and reception; from $20 a night; renovated November
    2023; nightly, monthly and short-term rates; Street 172) stand without a note. Everything the
    mockup added on top is marked TODO and must be confirmed by reception before the site goes
    live: the Double and Suite prices, the room sizes and what is in the rooms, the check-in and
    check-out times, the airport transfer, and the dishes on the board.

    The booking box is a plain GET form: no circuit, no JavaScript. It lands on /book with the
    dates and the number of guests in the address, and Book.razor takes it from there.
*@

<PageTitle>NFHotel &amp; Bar — Street 172, Phnom Penh</PageTitle>

<div class="pub-hero">
    <div class="pub-wrap">
        <h1><span class="pub-logo-mark">NF</span>Hotel</h1>
        <p class="pub-hero-sub">Hotel &amp; bar &middot; Street 172, Phnom Penh</p>
        <p class="pub-hero-tag">Beds from $20 a night. Bar and kitchen open 24 hours.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="pub-hero-pic">
    <img src="@Assets["img/facade.svg"]" alt="Drawing of the front of NFHotel on Street 172 at dusk, with the bar lit up and a tuk-tuk parked outside" />
</div>

<div class="pub-wrap">
    <div class="pub-bookbox">
        <form method="get" action="/book">
            <div class="field">
                <label class="field-label" for="home-check-in">Check-in</label>
                <input class="field-input numeric" id="home-check-in" name="checkIn" type="date" min="@Today" value="@DefaultCheckIn" required />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="field-label" for="home-check-out">Check-out</label>
                <input class="field-input numeric" id="home-check-out" name="checkOut" type="date" min="@Tomorrow" value="@DefaultCheckOut" required />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="field-label" for="home-guests">Guests</label>
                <select class="field-select" id="home-guests" name="guests">
                    <option value="1">1</option>
                    <option value="2" selected>2</option>
                    <option value="3">3</option>
                    <option value="4">4</option>
                </select>
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Check availability</button>
            <p class="pub-bookbox-note">The day you leave doesn't count as a night. No booking fee, pay on arrival.</p>
        </form>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pub-section" id="welcome">
    <div class="pub-wrap pub-welcome">
        <div class="pub-prose">
            <h2>Welcome</h2>
            <p>
                NFHotel is a small hotel and bar on Street 172, in the old part of Phnom Penh between
                the riverside and the Central Market. The rooms were fully renovated in November 2023.
                They are quiet, the beds are good, and they start at $20 a night.
            </p>
            <p>
                Downstairs, the bar and the kitchen are open all day and all night, and there is always
                someone at reception. A lot of our guests stay for a while, so we have nightly, monthly
                and short-term rates. If you are staying a week or more, email us and we will sort out a price.
            </p>
            @* TODO: the list repeats placeholders from the mockup (check-in times, luggage storage); confirm with reception. *@
            <ul>
                <li>Check-in from 2 pm, check-out by noon</li>
                <li>Air-con and hot water in every room</li>
                <li>Free Wi-Fi in the rooms and the bar</li>
                <li>Pay when you arrive, cash or card</li>
                <li>Two minutes' walk to the river</li>
                <li>Luggage storage before and after your stay</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <figure class="pub-illus">
            <img src="@Assets["img/bar.svg"]" alt="Drawing of the bar at night: bottles on the shelves, three lamps over the counter" />
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pub-section pub-section-soft" id="rooms">
    <div class="pub-wrap">
        <h2>Our rooms</h2>
        <p class="pub-intro">
            Three kinds of room over three floors. All of them have air-con, a private bathroom with
            hot water, Wi-Fi and daily cleaning. Prices are per room per night, in US dollars.
        </p>

        @* TODO: the descriptions, sizes and what is in the rooms are placeholders. Only "from $20" is the hotel's own figure. *@
        <article class="pub-room">
            <figure class="pub-illus">
                <img src="@Assets["img/single.svg"]" alt="Drawing of a single room with a bed, a bedside lamp and a window with teal shutters" />
            </figure>
            <div class="pub-prose">
                <h3>Single room</h3>
                <p class="pub-room-price">From $20 a night <span>&middot; sleeps 1 &middot; about 14 m&sup2;</span></p>
                <p>
                    A single bed, a small desk by the window, a wardrobe and your own bathroom. Good if you
                    mostly need a quiet place to sleep and a cold shower after a day in the heat.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Single bed</li>
                    <li>Private bathroom, hot water</li>
                    <li>Air-con</li>
                    <li>Wi-Fi</li>
                    <li>Desk and wardrobe</li>
                    <li>Daily cleaning</li>
                </ul>
                <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/book?guests=1">Check availability</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pub-room">
            <figure class="pub-illus">
                <img src="@Assets["img/double.svg"]" alt="Drawing of a double room with a wide bed, two pendant lamps and a big window with shutters" />
            </figure>
            <div class="pub-prose">
                <h3>Double room</h3>
                @* TODO: $28 is a placeholder; the Manager's room rate (MIL-055) is the real figure. *@
                <p class="pub-room-price">From $28 a night <span>&middot; sleeps 2 &middot; about 20 m&sup2;</span></p>
                <p>
                    A double bed or two singles (say which when you book), a wardrobe and a window to the
                    street or to the quiet side. This is the room most people book.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Double bed or two singles</li>
                    <li>Private bathroom, hot water</li>
                    <li>Air-con</li>
                    <li>Wi-Fi</li>
                    <li>Fridge</li>
                    <li>Daily cleaning</li>
                </ul>
                <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/book?guests=2">Check availability</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pub-room">
            <figure class="pub-illus">
                <img src="@Assets["img/suite.svg"]" alt="Drawing of the suite, with a bed, a sofa, a coffee table and balcony doors onto the street" />
            </figure>
            <div class="pub-prose">
                <h3>Suite</h3>
                @* TODO: $45 is a placeholder; the Manager's room rate (MIL-055) is the real figure. *@
                <p class="pub-room-price">From $45 a night <span>&middot; sleeps up to 4 &middot; about 32 m&sup2;</span></p>
                <p>
                    The corner rooms on the top floor. A double bed, a sitting area with a sofa that two
                    children can sleep on, a bigger bathroom and the best view of the street. Popular for
                    families and for longer stays.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Double bed and sofa bed</li>
                    <li>Sitting area, desk</li>
                    <li>Bigger bathroom, hot water</li>
                    <li>Air-con</li>
                    <li>Wi-Fi, fridge</li>
                    <li>Daily cleaning</li>
                </ul>
                <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/book?guests=3">Check availability</a>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pub-section" id="food">
    <div class="pub-wrap pub-food">
        <div class="pub-prose">
            <h2>Food &amp; drink, around the clock</h2>
            <p>
                The kitchen doesn't close. Burgers, a few Khmer dishes, cold Cambodia draught and breakfast
                whenever you wake up, whether that is 7 in the morning or 4 in the afternoon.
            </p>
            <p>
                The board shows what is on in the evening and late at night. The full menu is at the bar,
                and the kitchen will make most of it at any hour.
            </p>
            <p><em>"Last call?" is not something you will hear here.</em></p>
            <figure class="pub-illus pub-illus-wide">
                <img src="@Assets["img/food.svg"]" alt="Drawing of a burger, a basket of fries and a draught beer on the bar counter" />
            </figure>
        </div>
        <MenuBoard />
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pub-section pub-section-soft" id="location">
    <div class="pub-wrap">
        <h2>Where we are</h2>
        <p class="pub-intro">
            We are on Street 172 in Daun Penh, two minutes' walk from the riverside and about ten from
            the Royal Palace. Click a place on the map to see what it is and how long it takes to get
            there from our front door.
        </p>
        <NeighbourhoodMap />
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pub-section" id="info">
    <div class="pub-wrap">
        <h2>Good to know</h2>
        @* TODO: check-in times, payment details and the airport transfer are placeholders until reception confirms them. *@
        <table class="pub-facts">
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Check-in and check-out</th>
                    <td>Check-in from 2 pm, check-out by 12 noon. Arriving in the middle of the night is fine, reception is awake. We can keep your luggage before and after.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Payment</th>
                    <td>When you arrive, in US dollars or riel, cash or card. No deposit and no booking fee. Small change comes back in riel (about 4,000 riel to the dollar).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">From the airport</th>
                    <td>Techo International Airport is about an hour away by taxi. Book a taxi at the counter in arrivals, or ask us and we will arrange a pick-up.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Getting around</th>
                    <td>Tuk-tuks are everywhere. The PassApp and Grab apps give you a fixed price so you don't have to haggle.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Weather</th>
                    <td>Dry and pleasant from November to February, hot in March and April, and rain most afternoons from June to October.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Longer stays</th>
                    <td>We have monthly and short-term rates. Email us with your dates and we will quote a price before you book.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Languages</th>
                    <td>English and Khmer at reception.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pub-section pub-section-soft">
    <div class="pub-wrap pub-prose">
        <h2>Book a room</h2>
        <p class="pub-intro">
            Pick your dates, choose a room and leave your details. Reception confirms your booking once
            we've seen it, usually within a few hours. You pay when you arrive, and there is no booking fee.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/book">Book your stay</a>
    </div>
</section>
